      against was always a single entry -- meaning the code that maps
      several arbiters onto a partition, dedupes them by parent and
      counts the ones being concurrently rebuilt had nothing to do.
      upsert_keys and partitioned_side now each carry a second unique
      index over the same column as the primary key, so EXPLAIN reports

        Conflict Arbiter Indexes: p_pkey, pgb_part_id_uniq

      on both the plain and the partitioned target.  8 runs of
      partitions at stressval 4 with that in place were clean, so it did
